                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I like the first game, but midway through this one I just uninstalled and I'm not gonna bother with the third game.\n\nI've never played an IF game that pissed me off as much as this one. The first moment that made me go \"what the fuck? Okay then...\" was an anticlimactic \"Sorry, you lose\" after not making the correct series of choices, forcing me to heavily penalize myself or restart the ENTIRE GAME. The second (and last moment) was Black Magic, a kind but flawed character, completely switching up for no reason and becoming a vindictive snake just... because? What's worse is you have a few lines of dialogue bringing up how out of character this is, but you can't do jack shit because the author doesn't know how to write arguments. Every confrontation ends with a hilarious \"we're done here\" and the character just walks away without resistance.\n\nBut hey, if you like repeatedly smashing your balls with a hammer in every choice you make (unless it's the one the author wants you to choose) and you like feeling useless, you'll probably really enjoy this game. A masochist's interactive fiction, if you will.",
